Here’s how you would invoke the helper to serialize your `userProfile` map while guaranteeing no self‑references and wrapping it with the proper JSON object delimiters:

```java
// Assuming `userProfile` is a java.util.Map<String,Object> containing:
//   name  -> String
//   age   -> Integer
//   email -> String

functions.XContentBuilder_map({
  values: "userProfile",          // the map you want to serialize
  ensureNoSelfReferences: "true", // avoid stack‑overflow from circular refs
  writeStartAndEndHeaders: "true" // emit `{` and `}` around the output
});
```

This call will produce an `XContentBuilder` that contains the serialized form of `userProfile`, complete with the opening `{` and closing `}` braces, and it will safely guard against any accidental self‑referencing entries in the map.

